[h1]Phobos Manufacturing[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.18.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - unpublished draft

Refining and chemistry aboard your ship: turn what the crew mines into water, metal stock, oxygen and fertiliser, and do something useful with the hydrogen. Outputs follow realistic chemistry within the game's units, and when it goes wrong, the game's own dangers apply.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Phobos' Fennmark V4 Volatiles Refinery[/b] (4 x 4, 24 kW): water from hydrates and clay hydrates, ammonia from salt crust, carbon stock from carbon ore (run a scrubber for its CO2, CO and smoke), nickel-iron ingots from meteoric iron, and CO2 from the LC-3's leached residue. With Shipbreaker it also makes steel ingots.
[*][b]Phobos' Fennmark X2 Chemical Processor[/b] (2 x 2, 6 kW): electrolysis, 1.125 kg of water an hour into 1 kg of oxygen (a canister or the cabin air) and 0.125 kg of hydrogen.
[*][b]Phobos' Fennmark K2 Sabatier Reactor[/b] (2 x 2, 1.2 kW): CO2 and hydrogen into water and methane. With the X2 it wins back about half the water, as NASA's Sabatier system on the ISS does.
[*][b]Phobos' Tolvane AX-2 Ammonia Cracker[/b] (2 x 2, 2 kW): stored ammonia into nitrogen for your cabin air and hydrogen, each to its own store.
[*][b]Phobos' Lixivar LC-3 Leach and Crystallise Unit[/b] (3 x 3, 12 kW): choose a recipe. It leaches an evaporite crust into potassium sulfate, phosphate and a residue, turns the phosphate and a little ammonia into struvite fertiliser and, with Agriculture, blends both into Groundwork makeup salts. Its water comes from a linked vessel and mostly goes back.
[*][b]Gas stores in three sizes[/b] for hydrogen, methane, oxygen, nitrogen, carbon dioxide and ammonia. Stations sell bulk oxygen, nitrogen and CO2 through Bulk supplies.
[*][b]Phobos' Fennmark P1 RCS Propellant Manifold[/b] (INSTALL > HVAC): feeds your thrusters from up to four gas stores, each gas at its real worth per kilogram. Every store starts switched off.
[*][b]Phobos' Fennmark L2 Canister Filling Station[/b] (INSTALL > HVAC): fills suit bottles and canisters to a safe 99% from your stores; Decant empties them. Right-click Keep suit bottles charged and the crew top up low bottles.
[*][b]Phobos' Fennmark A2 Cabin Air Regulator[/b] (INSTALL > HVAC): holds its room's oxygen and pressure from O2 and N2 stores. It only adds gas and never lets oxygen pass 30%.
[*]Clay hydrates, salt crust and evaporite crust turn up in C-class finds, in place of some silicates. Ores are mined, never bought.
[*]Prices, charges, materials and store ratings are data files you can override in BepInEx/config/PhobosManufacturing.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]This is late-game plant: the V4 costs 64,000 cr. Buy the machines at K-Leg, Venus, San Diego's Halvorson and regional supply kiosks, for scrip at CCRE and GalCon faction kiosks (Friendly or Trusted), or find one in engineering salvage. They install from INSTALL > APPS; none can be built.
[*]Water charges and the X2 need a Shipbreaker S3 to S5 silo or an Agriculture R3 to R5 reservoir within one tile.
[*]Right-click a machine and choose Control Panel. Link its vessel, store or canister under Connections, choose the LC-3's recipe, load one charge into the feed window, then choose Start.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.54.0 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Optional: Phobos Shipbreaker 0.38.0 or newer (S3 silo and the steel charge) and Phobos Agriculture (R3 reservoir, makeup salts). Water work needs one of them.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Manufacturing and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it so they load. Repeat after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[*]Used the repository's local installer before? Remove those copies first so only one loads. See the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/installing-mods.md]installation guide[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ordinary saves are supported. Keep required mods installed while a save uses their content. Updating does not refill existing shops.
[*]Working machines pause after a reload until you press Start, keeping charge and progress.
[*]Stored gases are kilogram records. Empty a store before removing it.
[*]A damaged hydrogen store leaks to space and, with oxygen and a spark, fire or working refinery, burns through the game's own explosion. A damaged methane store leaks into the room and burns to CO2; a damaged ammonia store leaks poison; a damaged K2 or AX-2 dumps its gas. Extra cabin oxygen raises the fire risk.
[*]A metal melt left waiting for a cool room too long freezes into slag. No crew loading orders yet.
[*]Automated checks pass; in-game checks pending.
[/list]

[h2]Credits and sources[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited in the guides. Research informs design; equipment sizes and operating limits are gameplay choices.
Every recipe conserves mass. Reactions, energies and hazards draw on NIST, NASA, the Dawn and OSIRIS-REx science teams and iron-meteorite mineralogy; yields rounded to item units are labelled as ours. The chemistry record cites each source beside its claim.
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production, including PixelLab; provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

